'''''Iron Man: Armored Adventures''''' (also known in early promotional materials as '''''Iron Man: The Animated Series''''') is a French-Luxembourgish-British-American 3D CGI-animated series based on the [[Marvel Comics]] [[superhero]] [[Iron Man]]. It debuted in the United States on [[Nicktoons (American TV channel)|Nicktoons]] on April 24, 2009, and it aired on [[Cartoon Network (Canada)|Teletoon]] in Canada.<ref>{{cite web|last=Findlay |first=Kurtis |url=http://www.animatedsuperheroes.com/2008/05/iron-man-armored-adventures.html |title=Iron Man: Armored Adventures |publisher=Animated Superheroes |date=2008-05-12 |access-date=2011-02-27}}</ref> The series is story edited by showrunner [[Christopher Yost]],<ref>{{cite web|url=http://marvel.com/news/moviestories.7265.2_New_Iron_Man~colon~_Armored_Adventures_Videos |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090321120908/http://www.marvel.com/news/moviestories.7265.2_New_Iron_Man~colon~_Armored_Adventures_Videos |url-status=dead |archive-date=March 21, 2009 |title=2 New Iron Man: Armored Adventures Videos &#124; Iron Man &#124; Movie & TV News &#124; News |publisher=Marvel.com |date=2009-03-18 |access-date=2011-02-27}}</ref> who also worked on ''[[Wolverine and the X-Men (TV series)|Wolverine and the X-Men]]'', and numerous other [[Marvel Animation]] projects. The television show is not related to the 2007 animated film ''[[The Invincible Iron Man (film)|The Invincible Iron Man]]''; it has a different voice cast, but some story elements are similar and the show uses the same musical score as the film in some instances. It is the first Iron Man television series since [[Iron Man (TV series)|''Iron Man'']] from 1994 to 1996 (and the last until ''[[Iron Man and His Awesome Friends]]'' in 2025), and started airing after the success of the [[Iron Man (2008 film)|live action ''Iron Man'' film]], which had been distributed by Nicktoons' sibling [[Paramount Pictures]].

The series follows the adventures of a younger version of Tony Stark and his [[alter ego]] of [[Iron Man]]. As Iron Man, he uses his technological inventions to fight other similarly technologically advanced threats. His friends [[War Machine|James "Rhodey" Rhodes]] and [[Pepper Potts]] help him on his courageous and dangerous adventures.

The second season of this series premiered on July 13, 2011, running concurrently with the English dub of the completely separate ''[[Marvel Anime|Marvel Anime: Iron Man]]'' anime series, which had already finished airing on Japan's [[Animax]] in 2010.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2010-05-28/iron-man-anime-us-debut-in-july-jp-debut-in-october | title=Iron Man Anime's US Debut in July, JP Debut in October| date=24 May 2023}}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url=http://www.c21media.net/resources/detail.asp?area=79&article=56347 | title=Marvel to behold}}</ref>

On August 25, 2012, it was revealed that ''Iron Man: Armored Adventures'' would air as part of [[The CW Television Network|The CW]]'s new Saturday morning children's block [[Vortexx]]. After November 24, 2012, [[Vortexx]] ceased airing the show and replaced it with ''[[Transformers: Prime]]'' on December 8, 2012.

As of May 2025, both seasons of the show are available on [[Disney+]] (as of January 2021) and [[Amazon Prime]] Canada via [[Crave (TV network)|Crave]].

==Synopsis==
{{Anchor|Plot}}
After a plane crash in which his industrialist father [[Howard Stark]] disappears after refusing to weaponize the Earth Mover at [[Iron Monger|Obadiah Stane]]'s behest, Tony Stark uses a high-tech suit of armor he has constructed and investigates a charge that Stane may have been involved in his father's death. As Iron Man, Tony spends his time stopping Stane's plans and saving the world from other villains, such as [[Mandarin (character)|Mandarin]], [[Fixer (Marvel Comics)|Mr. Fix]], [[Whiplash (Marvel Comics)|Whiplash]], [[Advanced Idea Mechanics|A.I.M.]], [[Living Laser]], the [[Maggia (comics)|Maggia]], [[Controller (Marvel Comics)|Controller]], [[Crimson Dynamo]], [[Blizzard (Marvel Comics)|Blizzard]], [[Killer Shrike]], [[Unicorn (Marvel Comics)|Unicorn]], [[MODOK]], [[Ghost (Marvel Comics)|Ghost]], [[Black Knight (Nathan Garrett)|Black Knight]], and [[Technovore]]. He is assisted in his crime fighting efforts by [[War Machine|James Rhodes]] and [[Pepper Potts]]. Tony's activities as Iron Man usually result in his needing to make up excuses as to why he is constantly late or missing from school and other activities. Dependent on his technology for survival, Tony must balance the pressures of teenage life with the duties of being a superhero.

===First season===
The first season of ''Iron Man: Armored Adventures'' has a total of 26 episodes. It focuses on Tony, Pepper, Rhodey, and [[Temugin|Gene Khan]] working together to find the five [[Mandarin's rings|Makluan rings]]. After overthrowing his stepfather Xin Zhang, Gene secretly works undercover to steal the rings from his friends, and ends up betraying them. At the end of the season, Gene discovers that there are five additional rings, while Tony learns that Howard survived, but was captured.

===Second season===
The second season of ''Iron Man: Armored Adventures'' has a total of 26 episodes, just like the first season.<ref name="Comic-Con 2010: Marvel Animation Panel">{{cite web|url=http://screenrant.com/marvel-animation-panel-comic-con-2010-kofi-69887/ |title=Comic-Con 2010: Marvel Animation Panel |publisher=Screenrant.com |date=2010-07-23 |access-date=2011-02-27}}</ref> [[Black Widow (Natasha Romanova)|Black Widow]], [[Hawkeye (Clint Barton)|Hawkeye]], [[Doctor Doom]], [[Magneto (Marvel Comics)|Magneto]], and [[Justin Hammer]] appear in this season.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://marvel.popgeeks.com/news.php?action=fullnews&id=676|title=New Stills, Series Description For "Iron Man: Armored Adventures" Season Two|access-date=July 16, 2011|author=James Harvey|publisher=Toon Zone.net}}{{Dead link|date=March 2023 |bot=InternetArchiveBot |fix-attempted=yes }}</ref><ref>{{cite tweet|user=Marvel|number=27281675897|author=Marvel Entertainment|title=@RobbieNewton1 We'll confirm Doctor Doom is in IM:AA season 2! Anything else...keep waiting!|date=2010-10-13 |access-date=2020-06-13}}</ref>

The second season covers the [[Armor Wars]] saga and Stane International storylines, with Rhodey becoming War Machine during the first half of the season.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://marvel.toonzone.net/news.php?action=fullnews&id=675|title=Descriptions For Upcoming New Episodes Of "Iron Man: Armored Adventures"|access-date=July 26, 2011|author=James Harvey|publisher=Toon Zone.net|archive-date=October 22, 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121022170128/http://marvel.toonzone.net/news.php?action=fullnews&id=675|url-status=dead}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |author=James Harvey |title=New Images, Details For "Iron Man: Armored Adventures" October 2011 episodes |url=http://marvel.toonzone.net/news.php?action=fullnews&id=712 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20111005004908/http://marvel.toonzone.net/news.php?action=fullnews&id=712 |archive-date=October 5, 2011 |access-date=October 9, 2011 |publisher=Toon Zone.net}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.tvguide.com/tvshows/Iron-Man-2011/episode-4-season-2/ghost-machine/297143|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121021183829/http://www.tvguide.com/tvshows/Iron-Man-2011/episode-4-season-2/ghost-machine/297143|url-status=dead|archive-date=October 21, 2012|title=IMAA 2x4 on TVGuide|publisher=TVGuide}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://marvel.toonzone.net/news.php?action=fullnews&id=724|title=Marvel Animation Age - The Marvel Animation News Resource|website=marvel.toonzone.net|access-date=2011-11-02|archive-date=2012-12-13|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121213094111/http://marvel.toonzone.net/news.php?action=fullnews&id=724|url-status=dead}}</ref> Meanwhile, Gene forces Howard to help him find the remaining rings. In the second half of the season, Justin Hammer buys Stark International and Iron Man must stop him from weaponizing its projects.

In the series finale, Iron Man and various other heroes work to stop the Makluan aliens from destroying Earth.

