==Production==

===Pre-release===
Talks for a modern Iron Man animated series began in 2003 as a tie in with the proposed [[Nick Cassavetes]] directed Iron Man film at [[New Line Cinema]] alongside a Fantastic Four animated series that would eventually become [[Fantastic Four: World's Greatest Heroes]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=ICv2 |date=2003-11-23 |title=More Marvel Movie News |url=https://icv2.com/articles/comics/view/3922/more-marvel-movie-news |access-date=2026-04-28 |website=ICv2 |language=en}}</ref> Months before the series' television debut, Marvel had a screening of the first episode at [[San Diego Comic-Con]].<ref name="firstlook">{{cite web |date=July 14, 2008 |title=First Look: ''Iron Man: Armored Adventures'' Animated Series |url=http://marvel.com/news/moviestories.4184.First_Look~colon~_Iron_Man~colon~_Armored_Adventures |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20080715121012/https://www.marvel.com/news/moviestories.4184.First_Look~colon~_Iron_Man~colon~_Armored_Adventures |archive-date=July 15, 2008}}</ref> Additionally, several promotional videos were released on the Marvel website.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://marvel.com/news/moviestories.7668.Iron_Man~colon~_Armored_Adventures_Video_Spotlight_1 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090419130149/http://www.marvel.com/news/moviestories.7668.Iron_Man~colon~_Armored_Adventures_Video_Spotlight_1 |url-status=dead |archive-date=April 19, 2009 |title=Iron Man: Armored Adventures - Action and Adventure Video Spotlight &#124; Iron Man &#124; Movie & TV News &#124; News |publisher=Marvel.com |date=2009-04-16 |access-date=2011-02-27}}</ref>

===Theme song===
Popular rock band [[Rooney (band)|Rooney]] recorded the theme song to the series.<ref name="ThemeSong">{{cite magazine|last=Collis |first=Clark |url= https://ew.com/article/2009/03/27/iron-man-exclus/|title='Iron Man' exclusive! Watch Rooney's clip for their new Tony Stark theme song |magazine=Entertainment Weekly|date=2009-03-27 |access-date=2020-06-13}}</ref> The song originally could be downloaded from Teletoon's website. A provided "secret code", Tony, would be needed to access the theme. This "secret code" was shown onscreen during Canadian broadcasts of the first few episodes of the first season. The music video for the theme song features clips of Rooney singing, along with clips of Iron Man from the show.<ref name="ThemeSong"/>

===Animation style===
The series is made primarily using [[computer-generated imagery]] (CGI), in a similar style to ''[[Spider-Man: The New Animated Series]]''. The technique is similar to [[Cel-shaded animation|cel-shading]] animation technique, although the detail and resolution are lower.

==DVD releases==
===United States===
The pilot episode was released as a bonus feature in [[Wal-Mart]]'s DVD edition of ''[[Iron Man (2008 film)|Iron Man]]'' (2008).

Distribution rights to the series in North America was held by [[Gaiam Vivendi Entertainment|Vivendi Entertainment]].<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.ign.com/articles/2012/06/01/iron-man-armored-adventures-lands-on-dvd | title=Iron Man: Armored Adventures Lands on DVD | date=June 2012 }}</ref> Volume One was released on DVD in the United States on October 20, 2009. The Blu-ray edition was released exclusively through Best Buy Volume Two was released in the United States on January 5, 2010. These two releases were distributed through [[Genius Products|Genius Entertainment]]. The Complete Season One was released in the United States on May 4, 2010. The Complete Season One set included an unreleased pair of Volume Three and Four DVDs.

Season Two, Volume One was released on DVD on June 26, 2012, with Volume Two released on September 25, 2012.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.tvshowsondvd.com/news/Iron-Man-Armored-Adventures-Season-2-Volume-2/17149|title=Iron Man: Armored Adventures - Release Date, Cost for 'Season 2, Volume 2' on DVD|last=Lambert|first=David|date=June 26, 2012|work=[[TVShowsOnDVD]]|access-date=June 28, 2012|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120628195440/http://www.tvshowsondvd.com/news/Iron-Man-Armored-Adventures-Season-2-Volume-2/17149|archive-date=June 28, 2012}}</ref> The Season 2, Volume 3 DVD was released on January 22, 2013.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://marvel.com/news/story/19698/iron_man_armored_adventures_season_2_vol_3_coming_to_dvd|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121115100311/http://marvel.com/news/story/19698/iron_man_armored_adventures_season_2_vol_3_coming_to_dvd|url-status=dead|archive-date=November 15, 2012|title=Download Episode 303 of This Week in Marvel|website=News - Marvel.com}}</ref> Season 2 Volume 4 and the complete second season set became available April 23, 2013.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.amazon.com/Iron-Man-Armored-Adventures-Season/dp/B00AZL30TC|title=Iron Man: Armored Adventures - Season 2, Vol 4|date=23 April 2013|via=Amazon}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.amazon.com/Iron-Man-Armored-Adventures-Complete/dp/B00B9LNPUQ|title=Iron Man: Armored Adventures, Complete Season 2|date=23 April 2013|via=Amazon}}</ref>

===United Kingdom===
In the UK, distribution rights to the series were held by [[ITV Studios|ITV Global Entertainment]]. Volume One contains the first 13 episodes (the one-hour pilot being split into two separate episodes) on two discs.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.amazon.co.uk/dp/B0029KQNZ0 |title=Man: Armored Adventures DVD Vol. 1 at |date=7 September 2009 |publisher=Amazon.co.uk |access-date=2011-02-27}}</ref>

===Australia===
The complete first season was released on Blu-ray in Australia.

==Reception==
The hour-long premiere of ''Iron Man: Armored Adventures'' broke Nicktoons Network's record of highest-rated original series by premiering with over 125,000 viewers.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Hauman |first1=Glenn |title=Iron Man: Armored Adventures breaks Nicktoons rating record |url=https://www.comicmix.com/2009/04/29/iron-man-armored-adventures-breaks-nicktoons-rating-record/ |website=ComicMix |access-date=13 June 2020 |date=29 April 2009}}</ref>

Reviews of the pilot episode have been mixed. Some praise the series for its detailed and layered writing, strong continuity, and character designs. ''[[Entertainment Weekly]]'' gave the series debut a B+ grade, saying, "What could've been a clunky retrograde reboot works surprisingly well, thanks to some smart writing and stellar CG butt-kickery."<ref>Bernadin, Marc (2009-4-24). "Tonight's Best, April 24, 2009", ''Entertainment Weekly.''</ref>

===Awards===
In 2012, ''Iron Man: Armored Adventures'' won the Pulcinella Award for Best TV Series for Teens.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://marvel.toonzone.net/news.php?action=fullnews&id=786|title=Marvel Animation Age - The Marvel Animation News Resource|website=marvel.toonzone.net|access-date=2012-03-31|archive-date=2012-12-13|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121213094050/http://marvel.toonzone.net/news.php?action=fullnews&id=786|url-status=dead}}</ref>

In 2013, it was included on ''TV Guide'''s list of the 60 greatest cartoons of all time.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Sands |first1=Rich |title=The Definitive Ranking of The Simpsons, Peanuts, and More Old Cartoons From Your Childhood|url=https://www.tvguide.com/news/definitive-ranking-old-cartoons/ |website=TVGuide.com |access-date=13 June 2020 |date=9 October 2018}}</ref>

